WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.968
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:02.968
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.237
Thank you for being here.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.304
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:06.806
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.974
Happy Friday, everyone.

00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:10.143
This is very exciting.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:14.346
Tomorrow on NBC
is the 147 Kentucky Derby.

00:00:14.346 --> 00:00:16.282
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.650
Yep, the big race will feature

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.285
a bunch of three-year-olds
running around

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.187
while people just watch
and get drunk.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.488
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:24.490
It's like the sports version
of Zoom Kindergarten.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:26.192
[ Laughter ]
That's right.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:30.663
The current derby favorite
is Essential Quality, yeah.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:33.299
But there's an interesting horse
named Soup and Sandwich...

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.802
...that's owned by the heiress
to Campbell's Soup...

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:38.004
[ Laughter ]
-Ooh.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.907
...and it's rumored that,
if the horse loses,

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.709
he'll be...
-Oh, no.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.410
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.945
-Ugh!
-...fed some hay and say,

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:46.945
"Let's get 'em next year."

00:00:46.945 --> 00:00:47.947
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:48.947
-Put out to stud, yeah.

00:00:48.947 --> 00:00:50.483
-Well, guys, yesterday

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.285
President Biden
held a rally in Georgia and,

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.886
at the end of his speech,
he invited

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:55.888
a couple of senators
to join him onstage,

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:58.757
but he had a little trouble
finding his mask to put back on.

00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:00.593
[ Laughter ]
Watch him. Yeah, watch this.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:07.534
♪♪

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.634
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:11.603
♪♪

00:01:11.603 --> 00:01:12.771
-Looking for my mask.

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:13.807
I'm in trouble.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:16.542
-♪ I finally found you ♪

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:17.976
♪ Yes, that one ♪

00:01:17.976 --> 00:01:19.245
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.980
-Yeah.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.514
Right now,
the Pentagon's like, "Uh,

00:01:22.514 --> 00:01:24.450
maybe we should give
the nuclear codes to Jill.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.552
Uh..."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.421
You could practically hear
Jill thinking,

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.056
"If I have to go over there
and it's in this man's pocket...

00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:32.358
[ Laughter ]
I'm telling you.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.494
Joe, check your pocket."

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.928
Honestly, he's never been
more relatable

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:38.231
to every mask-wearing American
than at that very moment.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.632
You're like,
"You've got to be kidding me.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.634
I've been wearing
this dumb thing all day.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.901
Drive me nuts.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:45.237
This one was a tight,
uncomfortable one, too.

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:47.073
Where is it?"

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.807
I like how Biden timed
finding the mask

00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:51.110
to the lyrics of the song.
Did you see that?

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.745
That's not bad.
Can we see that again?

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.714
-♪ I finally found you ♪

00:01:55.714 --> 00:01:57.116
-Hey-oh!
-♪ Yes, that one ♪

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:58.251
-Like --

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:01.187
♪ I finally found you ♪

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.621
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:05.391
Then, he should've
Moonwalked out.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.393
Yeah, or did the Worm
or something.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.061
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:11.297
Right?
Nailed it.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.967
Meanwhile, in South Carolina,
former Vice President Mike Pence

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:17.303
gave his first speech
since leaving the White House

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.704
and a lot of people think
it was the start

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:21.040
of his campaign for 2024.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.143
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:26.912
Pence actually has a great
chance to unite the country

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:29.582
'cause both Biden and Trump
voters can't stand him.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.683
-Oh.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:33.686
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:34.854
[ Applause ]

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.555
See? Already.

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:37.990
-Took a while.
-Happening already.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.893
-Yeah. Took a while.
-But listen to this.

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:40.993
This is very interesting.
I heard that,

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:42.262
during Pence's speech,

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:45.164
only 55 people watched
on Facebook Live.

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:46.865
[ Ohhs and laughter ]

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:49.702
Fifty-five.
Not million

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.238
or 55,000.
-Ugh!

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.673
-Fifty-five people.

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.107
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:56.842
He's the only person
whose virtual events

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.210
have a 10% capacity.

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:01.114
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.848
Fifty-five people.

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:05.084
Some news from overseas --
today, Russia announced

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.719
that they produced
the world's first

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.587
COVID vaccine for animals...

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:09.922
[ Audience awws ]

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.590
...which means, pretty soon,
we'll have to deal

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:13.559
with animals posting
their vaccination cards

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:14.627
on social media.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.895
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:18.598
When the news broke,
Russian scientists were like --

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.698
[ Russian accent ]
Relax, relax.

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:21.567
We test on people, first.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:26.305
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:26.305 --> 00:03:28.608
I'm sure Russia's
animal vaccine is safe.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:30.209
They actually gave it
to one of the horses

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:31.944
in the Kentucky Derby.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.045
It's the number 6 horse,

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:34.713
Borscht or Sandwich.
-Oh.

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:38.017
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.818
[ Rimshot ]
-Come on!

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:42.021
-Wow.
-Come on. You got to do it.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.489
-Alright.
-You got to do it.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.758
[ Laughter ]
-Borscht or Sandwich.

00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:48.994
-Borscht or Sandwich.

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:51.930
Get this -- I saw that
Pope Francis just issued a law

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:54.300
that says Vatican employees
can't accept

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.304
any work-related gifts
more than $49.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.805
[ Laughter ]
When asked why

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:02.341
he issued the law,
Pope Francis said --

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:03.509
[ As Francis ]
Because it's funny.

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:08.881
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.916
The news really stunned
Vatican employees,

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:13.519
especially when the Pope
left the room on a hoverboard.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:19.025
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.627
That's right,
no more gifts over $49.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.829
And, now that the Church
has settled that issue,

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.430
there are officially
no more scandals.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:30.035
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:32.438
Some business news --
I saw that Lay's is releasing

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:34.306
new potato chips
that are dusted

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:36.642
with Cool Ranch Doritos
flavoring.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:39.111
[ Ohhs and laughter ]
They've even got
a great name for them --

00:04:39.111 --> 00:04:40.313
Cool Ranch Doritos.

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:44.550
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.919
And, finally, I saw that a man
in the Philippines holds

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.188
an interesting world record.
Watch this.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.958
-This guy, in the Philippines,
Percival Lugue,

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.292
started collecting toys

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:56.095
that came in fast food meals
when he was five.

00:04:56.095 --> 00:05:00.600
Fifty years later,
he's got about 20,000 of them.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.034
-It's like he's living
inside the world's biggest

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:03.136
claw machine.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:05.170
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.840
Meanwhile, that guy's family
hasn't had a happy meal

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.974
in 50 years.

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:10.442
"Clean it up!"

00:05:10.442 --> 00:05:12.611
Also, we're planning
something really fun

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:14.179
in honor of Mother's Day.

00:05:14.179 --> 00:05:16.115
We're going to team up
with our friends at Samsung

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:19.018
to celebrate some
amazing moms out there,

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:22.321
epic moms that have gone
above and beyond this past year.

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:23.922
We're going to do something
very special

00:05:23.922 --> 00:05:26.426
every single night next week,
so be sure to tune in for that.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:27.492
It's going to be a fun surprise.

00:05:27.492 --> 00:05:29.228
[ Cheering and applause ]

